## Architectural Significance

The Lender Process OS V2 demonstrates how complex lending decisions can be decomposed into bounded workflows without sacrificing consistency or traceability.

Normalization, validation, and routing remain separate operational responsibilities. Persistent state and standardized workflow contracts connect these responsibilities into a governed processing conveyor. This structure makes every material lending decision observable, reproducible, and available for downstream review.

